# Task 144-005-fix: ADR-008 Cycle 2 Fix — Priority Fix

## Baseline Analysis

Previous worker (144-005) created `src/core/session-interface.ts` with Connector class but:
1. Did NOT update `provider.ts` import (still imports from `../orchestra/connector.js`)
2. Did NOT convert `connector.ts` to re-export
3. Did NOT write tests
4. Docker worker exited without writing result file

## Solution

### Step 1: Update provider.ts import
- Line 6: `import { Connector } from '../orchestra/connector.js'` → `import { Connector } from './session-interface.js'`
- This breaks the core→orchestra cycle (ADR-008 violation)

### Step 2: Convert connector.ts to re-export
- Remove duplicate Connector/HealthCheckResult code
- Replace with: `export { Connector, HealthCheckResult } from '../core/session-interface.js'`
- Backward compatibility: all existing imports from `orchestra/connector.js` continue working

### Step 3: Tests
- `tests/core/session-interface.test.ts` — 12+ tests covering:
  - Connector constructor, registerProvider, getProvider
  - healthCheck (all, single, unregistered)
  - getAvailableProviders, isProviderReady
  - unregisterProvider, clear, size
  - checkAuthStatus (claude=ok, codex+gemini with/without env)
  - HealthCheckResult interface shape

### Step 4: Verification
- `tsc --noEmit` → clean
- `npx vitest run` → all pass
- `grep -l "from.*orchestra/connector" src/core/` → 0 (ADR-008 fix confirmed)

## Risk: LOW
- Re-export pattern ensures all external imports unchanged
- Only internal core/ import path changes
